   "body": "This PR is much more like a hotfix which solve the multi-open problem, but it seems will cause another problem: **Nothing will be shown when the command be called with another unfocused (also unrestored) 'Simple Browser' tab exist**. Because you just *return* in this condition.\r\n\r\nWhat's more:\r\n1. `vscode.window.tabGroups.activeTabGroup.tabs` is instanceof `Tab` instead of `TabGroup`. And I will use `tab` to represent the item of `tabs` below.\r\n\r\n2. You use the `tab.label === SimpleBrowserView.title` to implement the function of `existInTabGroup`, but in fact, I can easily create a file called 'Simple Browser' and open it as a tab with label=='Simple Browser'. The below video has shown this point. I suggest to use the `tab.input.viewType`.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/microsoft/vscode/assets/150506715/50c0b8fa-bbdd-45e0-9097-b7bad8fd4e79\r\n\r\nAt last, I have a solution at https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/182795#issuecomment-2177986195\r\nand https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/182795#issuecomment-2180172928 .\r\n\r\nBut I have some trouble on implementation.\r\n",
   "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
